--- WHAT SHIPPED (parity port of the web MapTileLayer) ---
4-file shared-surface pattern, bound to the shared P1/S8 seam + P1/S10 i18n facade; the view performs no query /
HTTP itself and reads every label from the projection. The web MapTileLayer selects a Leaflet TileLayer URL +
attribution from useQuery(['map-config'], getMapConfig) (free community tiles by default; Azure / Google tiles
when a provider + key are configured). Natively the base raster tiles are painted by the shared TsMapControl
(the Leaflet MapContainer analogue, Components/Maps — out of scope, reused) configured from the resolved
MapConfig, and this surface adds the data-binding layer + the full state matrix on top:
  * MapTileLayer.Model.cs      — MapTileLayerVisualState enum; MapTileLayerSnapshot (+ FromRepositoryResult adapter
                                 mapping the cache-then-network RepositoryResult<MapConfig> -> state + resolved
                                 TileSource via Core MapTileProvider, free-tile fallback exactly like the web
                                 `tiles = freeTiles` default); MapTileLayerRegistration (Slug, 6 automation ids,
                                 freshness window = web 5-min staleTime, 3 Fluent glyphs, 12 i18n keys + English
                                 fallbacks, ClassifyState + Provider/Style label helpers); the pure
                                 MapTileLayerProjection (per-state overlay/chip gates, localized strings,
                                 attribution, accessible name — provider key never enters it); and the PII-safe
                                 MapTileLayerDiagnostics (emits only `view.opened slug=MapTileLayer`).
  * MapTileLayer.Source.cs     — P1/S8 seam IMapTileLayerSource (web useQuery result) with an in-memory Static impl
                                 and a Repository impl over a cache-then-network stream (generation-guarded pump,
                                 + SetStyle re-projection for the web `style` prop without re-fetching).
  * MapTileLayer.ViewModel.cs  — INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable holder projecting Source -> Projection,
                                 RequestRefresh() forwarding (web query.refetch()), subscription cleanup.
  * MapTileLayer.cs            — WinUI 3 ContentControl hosting TsMapControl + state overlays: busy spinner
                                 (loading), TsErrorDisplay + Retry (error), stale / offline status chips, empty
                                 note, and a TsFullscreenButton (the web @/components/ui/FullscreenButton, mapped
                                 to its native counterpart, parity with MapFullscreenControl). Tokenized brushes
                                 (DisplayTokens, P1/S9) — no inline hex; reduce-motion honoured (entrance
                                 transition only when OS animations are enabled).

STATES REPRODUCED (every one renders — the web surface fetches, so it carries the full matrix): loading (busy
overlay over free tiles), ready (configured provider tiles, no chrome), empty (free community tiles + note),
error (free fallback + error overlay + retry), stale (cached config past freshness -> stale chip), offline
(cached config + offline chip). The base tiles always paint (the web renders the TileLayer immediately and swaps
providers when the query resolves). Accessibility: provider+style accessible name on the root; automation ids on
map/loading/error/status/fullscreen; polite live-region announcement on the status chips; the API key is consumed
only by the tile renderer and is asserted to never reach the accessible name / diagnostics. Telemetry:
view.opened slug=MapTileLayer (P1/S11).

i18n (P1/S10): every surface-owned string flows through ILocalizer with an English fallback. The web source has
NO t() calls — its only literals are the brand tile attributions (CARTO / OpenStreetMap / Esri / OpenTopoMap /
Azure Maps / Google Maps), which the provider terms require verbatim and which are intentionally NOT localized
(carried as Core TileSource.Attribution). Keys introduced for the WinUI catalogue (translation.mapTileLayer.*):
loading, error.title, error.message, retry, fullscreen, stale, offline, empty, accessibleName, provider.{community,
azure,google}, style.{dark,satellite,streets,terrain}. Following the established sibling convention (ServiceStatus
0xxx etc.) the keys + fallbacks live as asserted Registration constants resolved through the facade; no catalog
file edit was required (and the allowed-files scope is the surface folder).

