PRE-REQ REPAIR #2 (Breadcrumbs vs LayoutBreadcrumbs type collision): once the csproj loaded, the App project AND
the Tests project both failed to compile (30 errors: CS0101/CS0111/CS8863 + a cascaded CS0535) because the
Breadcrumbs surface (0167) and the LayoutBreadcrumbs surface (0170) BOTH defined BreadcrumbItem,
IBreadcrumbNavigator and NullBreadcrumbNavigator in the flat namespace TeslaSync.App.SharedSurfaces — a
pre-existing integration-merge collision that had been masked because the corrupted csproj aborted every
solution build before compilation. It is unrelated to MapTileLayer but blocks the entire Tests assembly (hence my
own MapTileLayer tests) from compiling. Resolved minimally + surgically by renaming the LayoutBreadcrumbs
surface's three colliding types to Layout-prefixed names (LayoutBreadcrumbItem / ILayoutBreadcrumbNavigator /
NullLayoutBreadcrumbNavigator) across its 4 surface files + its test (the Breadcrumbs surface keeps the canonical
names); grep verified those 3 names are referenced only within each surface's own files, so there is zero
external-reference risk. This also cleared the CS0535 (LayoutBreadcrumbsTests.FakeNavigator), which was purely a
collision artifact (its Navigate-only interface had been bound to Breadcrumbs' Prefetch-bearing interface).

